        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Aldrich, Bette Davis, Olivia de Havilland, Joseph Cotten, Agnes Moorehead, Mary Astor\n- Products: Vera Cruz, Kiss Me Deadly, The Big Knife, What Ever Happened to Baby Jane?, Hush...Hush, Sweet Charlotte\n- Roles: film director, writer, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Burgess Aldrich was born on August 9, 1918, and died on December 5, 1983.\n- Robert Aldrich was an American film director, writer, and producer.\n- Robert Aldrich was notable for the films Vera Cruz (1954), Kiss Me Deadly (1955), The Big Knife (1955), and What Ever Happened to Baby Jane?.\n- Hush...Hush, Sweet Charlotte is a 1964 American psychological thriller film directed and produced by Robert Aldrich.\n- Hush...Hush, Sweet Charlotte stars Bette Davis, Olivia de Havilland, Joseph Cotten, Agnes Moorehead, and Mary Astor.\n- Hush...Hush, Sweet Charlotte was Mary Astor's final film role.",
